  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Who enqueues (runtime)",
      "items": [
        "sources: extract (snapshot_service.py:287), profile (profiling_service.py:182), pii_scan (pii_scan_service.py:120), infer_relationships (relationship_service.py:152).",
        "files: index_document and reindex_documents (search.py:696, 950, 1036).",
        "assistant: assistant_task through the start_job tool (assistant/internal/tools.py:2120).",
        "All go through JobService.submit; the job row is the only queue (no broker)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Transition details",
      "items": [
        "worker claims: highest priority, oldest first; FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED so two workers never take one job.",
        "error or worker lost: handler exception, no handler for the type, or stale heartbeat without a usable checkpoint (or after 3 runs).",
        "worker lost, checkpoint: fail_lost requeues a stale job that saved a checkpoint, until it has run MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3 times.",
        "cancel while running: the handler sees ctx.cancelled and raises JobCancelledError; execute keeps the cancelled status."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Who runs (wiring)",
      "items": [
        "API uses QueuedJobRunner: submit only leaves the row queued (app.py:106-108).",
        "worker registers the same handlers (job_handlers.register_job_handlers) and loops: fail_lost, then claim_next until empty, then sleep worker_poll_seconds (worker.py:55-104).",
        "Tests use InlineJobRunner, which runs the job after the caller's transaction commits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Failure handling",
      "items": [
        "Retries are not automatic for handler errors: only a lost worker with a checkpoint is requeued.",
        "A lost job that is failed also calls the type's on_abandoned hook (document index / reindex register one).",
        "Stale after 60 s without heartbeat by default; the worker passes settings.job_stale_seconds."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Uncertain",
      "items": [
        "What each handler does on cancel mid-run depends on how often it checks ctx.cancelled; not traced per handler.",
        "Which handlers raise JobPausedError was not traced; the assistant task is the likely one (it asks the creator), unverified."
      ]
    }
  ]
